; The GEMM example: the OxCaml kernel, and the tile catalog naming the shapes,
; the size-to-shape choice, and the binding each shape maps to.
;
; matmul_tiled.ml is the kernel. It is OxCaml source with mode syntax that
; ordinary OCaml cannot parse, so it is absent from (modules) and compiled only
; by tools/compile_oxcaml_kernels.sh. No IR is built here.

(library
 (name oxgpu_matmul)
 (modules matmul_config)
 (libraries oxgpu)
 (wrapped false))
